hunger  is ravaging the young of yemen only the  most critical are taken in here  there are just far too many children to  care for  [Music]  and this is what malnutrition does to a  young body  it strips it down and opens it to  infection  chalmers spent just four years on earth  and there can be few days when she  hasn't been hungry  now she's terribly weak unable to stand  walk or talk  malnutrition destroys the body slowly  and cruelly  sharma's been in hospital for 16 days  already she's much better than when she  first came in  her younger sister has died here in the  year 2020  her mother's now desperately worried  about a second child  dying of starvation  i'm very scared i'm going to lose her  like i lost my other daughter she says  anxious family members wait outside many  have spent the six years of yemen's  civil war  running from the fighting the country is  devastated and it's the children who are  paying for years of political inaction  eighty percent of the population depend  on aid  to live worries over the coronavirus  epidemic  are utterly dwarfed by the fear of  having no food to keep your child alive  and every day here is a battle to keep  on breathing  on every single bed there's a tale of  tragedy  the sheer misery and desperation is  unavoidable  young males gasp for air and hang on by  a thread to life  zaid has cerebral palsy in a country  suffering the world's  worst humanitarian disaster his  condition is made horribly worse by lack  of nutrition  and over-stretched medical facilities  malnutrition babies lead to this  this situation now  little brother is here too but this is  actually better than they used to  they've moved four times to escape  fighting and help is hard to come by  international funding's been cut with  human rights groups  accusing the warring parties of  hampering the aid delivery  and so today they did not give a speech  our tents  we have difficult life also because of  the flooding  our situation is very bad  zay